{"summary":"Accepted the amendments that fix real correctness or test-strength defects, and rejected the ones that conflate distinct model knobs or misclassify seeded stochastic/factor-space heuristics as bugs.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-8dc1f3dd","decision":"reject","rationale":"`egg_oxygen_reference_mg_l` is documented and tested as an egg-development hatch-success parameter, not the adult-condition oxygen normalization. Reusing it in `update_condition()` would couple two distinct biological controls; if adult-condition DO should be configurable, it should get its own parameter rather than being forced to track the egg-specific one."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-5e14a754","decision":"reject","rationale":"The diagnostic checks operate on normalized factors (`f_oxygen`, `f_tan`, `f_no2`, etc.), and those factors already move when the underlying runtime parameters are retuned. That means the raw chemistry values at which the diagnostics fire are not stale in the way claimed; the hardcoded factor cutoffs are arguable heuristics, but not a correctness bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-68de6649","decision":"reject","rationale":"The egg-drop path is seeded RNG, so it is reproducible for a fixed simulation seed, and Bernoulli clutch loss under acute instability is a defensible modeling choice distinct from the deterministic smoothing used for expected transfers like spawning and hatching. Replacing it with `deterministic_transfer_count()` would materially change behavior more than it fixes a defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-2d9371fc","decision":"accept","rationale":"Counting only `ShrimpBerried` events does not prove three completed reproductive cycles, because those clutches can still be dropped or fail before producing juveniles. The existing population-growth assertion shows some success, but it does not establish three end-to-end cycles, so the test should verify hatching or an equivalent completion signal."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-3662d749","decision":"accept","rationale":"This is a real path-dependence bug: the same alkalinity stoichiometry is sourced from the exact constant in runtime defaults but from rounded literals in preset/scenario loading. Even though the numeric delta is small, construction path should not change the simulated chemistry for the same nominal preset, so the value should come from one source of truth."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-09646071","decision":"accept","rationale":"The trace pairs alkalinity consumption with a nitrogen metric based on nitrate production, but alkalinity depletion is driven by TAN oxidation. When nitrite accumulates, those quantities diverge, so the emitted pair can be scientifically misleading; the trace should emit the TAN-oxidized basis or otherwise align the nitrogen quantity with the alkalinity quantity."}]}